          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I am 34 weeks pregnant with swelling in my hands and a headache that will not shift. How urgent is this, and what should I be asking about?",
          "answer": "**Act today. Call your maternity or obstetric triage line now, and go to the nearest emergency department if any warning sign below appears.**\n\nThe risk tool returned a routine tier, but it did not match any pattern in its table, and it says that is not a clearance. The retrieved guidance on headache also says a new headache in pregnancy, \"particularly with visual changes, swelling or upper abdominal pain,\" needs same-day medical assessment (*Sudden severe headache and other dangerous headache patterns*). You have a new headache and swelling at 34 weeks, so you should be assessed today, not left for a routine appointment.\n\n**Go to emergency care immediately (call your local emergency number if you cannot get to hospital safely) if you have:**\n- Blurred vision, flashing lights, spots, or any loss of vision\n- Pain in the upper abdomen or under the right ribs\n- Severe or worsening headache, or confusion\n- Vomiting that will not stop\n- Shortness of breath or chest pain\n- A seizure or fit\n- Bleeding, fluid leaking from the vagina, or a sharp drop in your baby's movements\n\nThe first two items are named in the retrieved guidance. The others are standard safety advice from general medical knowledge, not from the documents I searched.\n\n**What the retrieved material does and does not cover:** My searches did not return a document on preeclampsia or other pregnancy-specific causes of headache and swelling, so I cannot describe that differential from the sources. The matching material was about migraine, colds and flu, which do not explain this combination well, and I won't guess beyond it. The symptom-grouping tool also failed, so I have no system-by-system breakdown. Only a clinician can assess what is causing your symptoms.\n\n**Questions to ask the triage line or your clinician today:**\n1. Given that I am 34 weeks pregnant, do I need to be seen in person today?\n2. Should my blood pressure be checked now, and should I have urine and blood tests?\n3. Is this headache different from any I have had before, and does it need an urgent scan or assessment?\n4. Is my swelling just in my hands, or should I be checked for swelling in my face or legs?\n5. Should I be monitored for the baby's wellbeing today?\n6. What symptoms should make me come in straight away rather than phone first?\n\nDo not take any painkiller or other medicine for the headache until you have spoken to a clinician, because some medicines are unsuitable in pregnancy and can hide symptoms that need checking.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
